# Data provenance

`DATA_SOURCES.txt` at the repo root is the single record of where every number,
geometry and map tile comes from. It must never go stale.

## Update it in the same change

Whenever you add, remove, re-point or re-label a data source, edit
`DATA_SOURCES.txt` in the same change. That includes:

- a new or changed API endpoint, query parameter, or base URL
- a new bundled asset under `public/asset/` (KML, JSON, HTML panel)
- a new basemap, label or DEM tile provider
- a figure hard-coded from a publication (add it to section 5 with a source URL
  and your confidence in that source)
- a change to a derived calculation, its constants, or its output values
  (update section 6 so drift is visible)
- resolving any "TO CONFIRM" item

Always append a dated line to the CHANGE LOG at the end of the file.

## Record these fields

What the data is · exact endpoint or file path · which source file consumes it ·
auth and attribution · the UI provenance label · the caveats.

## Be honest about quality

Distinguish measured, modelled, derived and synthetic data. The UI labels are
`Live · GloFAS`, `Live · ECMWF`, `Model`, `Estimated` and `Demo/Synthetic`; use
the same vocabulary in the file. If something is synthetic or unvalidated, say
so plainly rather than softening it — several parts of this app are demo data,
and section 8 lists claims that must not be made about the flood zones.
